10
00:58:49,411 --> 00:58:55,411
The Last Rifleman is a 2023 British drama film written by Kevin Fitzpatrick, loosely based
on real events and directed by Terry Loane, which features Pierce Brosnan.

11
01:04:42,352 --> 01:04:48,352
It follows Artie Crawford (Brosnan), a Northern Irish World War II veteran who, on the 75th anniversary of the D-Day landings in Normandy, decides to secretly escape his care home and
embarks on an arduous but inspirational journey from Northern Ireland to France, to pay his final respects to his best friend and find the courage to face the ghosts of his past.

12
01:10:35,294 --> 01:10:41,294
The film is loosely based on the true story of British D-Day veteran Bernard
Jordan, who left his care home in England to travel to France.

13
01:16:28,235 --> 01:16:34,235
Another film based on Jordan's story, The Great Escaper, starring
Michael Caine, was released a few weeks earlier.

14
01:22:21,176 --> 01:22:27,176
The Last Rifleman marked the final film appearance by John
Amos prior to his death on August 21, 2024.

15
01:28:14,117 --> 01:28:20,117
The film did not have a theatrical release; it premiered on the
Sky Cinema subscription service on 5 November 2023.

16
01:34:07,058 --> 01:34:13,058
The tone is emotional.
